A||||4||scotkb75||88 4 cyl with bad oil pump, what options??||||5||
Z||000000||scotkb75||11-05-2001||02:12 AM||||Just picked up a 1988 with the 4 cyl that is supposed to have a bad oil pump.  Apparently this engine has a special pump and balancer??  What are my options?  Low cost first, maybe 4.9 caddy engine down the road..||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||11-05-2001||07:24 AM||||Hey Scott!<BR>If you are planning the caddy, then do it...<BR>Don't waste money on a stop-gap engine...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||11-05-2001||09:18 AM||||Are you sure it's the oil pump? <BR>I've seen several 88 2.5's that just had a bad sender. Showed "0" oil pressure. <BR>Try measuring with a mechanical gauge before you do any expensive work.<BR>If it's knocking and clattering, nevermind.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-05-2001||07:55 PM||||If it really is bad, just shove another 4 used 4 cyl in it. You can get them from several GM cars fairly cheap. You'll need to put all the Fiero brackets and pulleys on but it beats the hell out of fixing an iffy motor.<P>that or just park it untill you can afford the conversion.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||scotkb75||11-05-2001||11:09 PM||||Thanks, I'll keep my eyes open at the "pull-n-save".  I saw a tech 4 2.5l a week ago Friday and when I went back Sat morning to get it, it was gone!  $135 for complete engine with only 88K miles... I thought that was a fair deal.||||reg||1
